<title>USA: STC, Centocor enter partnership.</title>
<headline>STC, Centocor enter partnership.</headline>
<dateline>BETHLEHEM, Pa. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>STC Technologies Inc, a leader in the development of detection technology, said it entered a strategic partnership with Centocor Inc to provide infectious disease screening kits to blood banks and plasma centers in the United States.</p>
<p>The agreement to distribute Centocor's syphilis and cytomegalovirus (CMV) assays allows STC to expand its product line to the blood bank and plasma industry, STC said.</p>
<p>This screening will help to identify patients or donors who have experienced infection of these prevalent conditions, which could, affect the blood supply, the company said.</p>
</text>
